ntire sword  tutorial in the beginning  originally egas the sparring hall  instructor would scold you for just  sneaking out with the sword  and after learning about your loft wing  going missing would agree to let you  take it after you go through some sword  practice  now you don't have to actually do the  sword practice after the dash tutorial  with instructor horwell he'll ask you if  you can retrieve the headmaster's pet  mia from the roof  in the original game once you do that  horwell will just thank you  but in the hd version horwell gives you  a reward of 20 rupees  in the original game when you're looking  for your loft wing pippit will mark the  location of the waterfall on your map  because fledge overheard gruse and his  buddies say that they were planning to  hide link's loft wing near a waterfall  after pippit does this he asks link if  he knows how to use his map and hit the  plus button to access it  however in skyward sword hd the map  tutorial actually happens sooner with  the headmaster putting an x on your map  to show where the plaza is and telling  you that you can use the minus button to  access your map  in the original game you just had to  find the plaza yourself after the  headmaster mentions it  the design of the hearts in the upper  left corner has changed and shrunk and  the ruby display has been moved from the  top left to the bottom left of the  screen  the shield icon underneath the hearts  will glow every now and again when it  was just a static image in the original  game  the face icons on the map have changed  and in my opinion they look a lot  creepier  when flying your loft wing the giant b  button with the words slow down  underneath has been removed from the  on-screen display  the lighting inside the thunderhead has  changed and it's easier to see that it's  raining  the spirit vessel graphic has moved up  the screen ever so slightly  you can now skip cutscenes in the base  game by hitting minus this functionality  did exis