 link didn't screw up  but this is a video game and not a real  life situation and yes  phi has been toned down a little bit in  this game you can't exactly remove  phi entirely since their personality is  shaped in a very specific way and they  talk in a very specific way but the  developers did fix it a bit to let you  as the player figure things out more  a little more frequently so now in some  situations where fi would pop out  automatically in the original game  the sword will glow prompting you to  summon phi by hitting down on the d-pad  but you don't have to  the power is in your hands i won't list  off every situation for spoiler reasons  but here are a few instances where i  noticed fi didn't pop out automatically  like the original  the first situation is after you get  your shiny green outfit and head into  town  phi still tells you about how the column  of light that appeared created an  opening in the cloud barrier  and phi still recommends getting a  shield and potions before heading to the  surface  but in the original game phi also  mentions that you can change the  on-screen interface to remove stuff like  the giant wii remote in the hd remaster  fi doesn't mention this and you can  change the setting to simple from the  very beginning  the next situation that was removed is  before you dive into that green column  of light  five pops out to tell you that the green  pillar is a column of light that marks  the point where you can descend to the  surface  didn't phy just say that next up in the  original game  when you first encounter kiwi phi  mentions that your dowsing ability is  picking up the kikui as zelda despite  the kikui not being zelda and you should  follow the creature and investigate  guess it was kind of obvious that you  should follow the kikui running away  from you  and then when you use the slingshot to  bring down the vine to get into the deep  woods  phi would originally pop out to  basically explain to you what you just  did  and how to use the weapon you literally  just used the last one i'll mention is  right before the skyview temple  phi warns you that they detect zelda's  aura in the giant temple in front of you  and that there are numerous monsters  inside and asks if you want to proceed  and you actually have to say yes or no  if you say yes which i did of course  phi says not to be overconfident and if  you feel unprepared  you can return to the sky and get a  shield and potions you know  the same thing phi said earlier before  we even left the sky  in total i counted 17 situations where  phi's dialogue was changed or removed  entirely  if you want to know the others let me  know in the comments and i'd be happy to  write them out  or if you found some yourself then leave  those in the comments as well  it's possible that i missed some number  eight amiibo functionality  alongside the release of skyward sword  hd nintendo is releasing a zelda and  loftwing amiibo figure  the way the amiibo figure works is you  tap it when you're on the surface and  then you will immediately be transported  to the sky  instead of having to look for a bird  statue to do it then when you use the  amiibo again in the sky it'll return you  to the exact location where you tap the  amiibo on the surface  it even works in buildings and dungeons  unfortunately we did not have access to  the zelda and loftwing amiibo figure  before launch so i was not able to test  this functionality myself  you actually won't be able to use this  amiibo figure until after you've saved  gorko from the bokoblins and head to  farron woods for the first time  phi will pop out and let you know that  you can return to the sky and use the  amiibo to do it  amiibo are off by default in the  settings so you'll have to enable it  once phi mentions this  to use the amiibo hit down on the d-pad  to summon phi  and if you have amiibo enabled the  bottom left option will be to use amiibo  also yes i tried using a bunch of other  amiibo i own including the skyward sword  link amiibo and none of them work  fide just says the amiibo accessory is  one they can't recognize  oh well number nine increased frame rate  the legend of zelda skyward sword hd  runs at 60 frames per second making it a  much smoother experience overall  the original skyward sword on the other  hand only ran at 30 frames per second  skyward sword hd is also the second  zelda game to ever run at 60 frames per  second with the first being a link  between worlds on 3ds  i realize this section is kind of short  but the jump from 60fps to 30fps is a  big deal and i hope future zelda games  are also 60fps  number 10 fast forward dialogue in  skyward sword hd you can now hit the b  button to fast forward the dialogue  which was not an option in the original  game  this is great for replays or speed runs  as well as situations where you  accidentally engage with the character  again and are forced to read the same  dialogue  if you're playing this game for the  first time it might not be the biggest  deal in the world but it's a very nice  quality of life update that i'm glad  exists  number 11 streamlined item information  in the original skyward sword every time  you quit the game and then came back  all the same collectibles you'd gotten  before would re-explain themselves and  force you to not only read the text you  already read but wait as it would show  you the item count go up in your  inventory so either you left the system  on and never saved and quit  or you dealt with it hope you like  reading about how monster claws are  extremely sharp and look painful to even  touch for the millionth time  thankfully in skyward sword hd this was  removed just like how it was removed in  twilight princess hd  the first time you read the text is the  only time you read the text even if you  save and quit a bunch of times and i'd  argue we're all more thankful for it  however for the individual gratitude  crystals you can collect this has not  changed with the dialogue popup and item  count animation happening all 15 times  thankfully you can at least fast forward  the text this time i also want to note  that when you get an item from a chest  it will still explain itself again  but it won't show the item count going  up in your inventory so that's a little  better i guess  either way this is one of the better  changes for sure number 12  hero mode doesn't overwrite your save  files this last big change  may not seem significant for those  unaware but it actually makes a major  difference  let me explain in the original skyward  sword once you beat the game you'd  unlock hero mode  hero mode is a harder version of the  game where enemies do double damage and  there are no recovery hearts among other  things  so after watching the final cut scenes  the game would say you can play again in  hero mode using the save data do you  want to continue  and if you select yes it would hit you  with your progress up to this point will  be deleted  are you sure you want to play hero mode  uh  maybe not if you were unaware this was  about to happen you'd either have to  bite the bullet and delete your save so  this could overwrite it  or you'd have to copy your save file on  the title screen before the final boss  and then defeat the final boss on the  new file  and overwrite said file so you can keep  your original and the new hero mode save  since skyward sword hd allows you to  save on any save slot at any time  this situation has thankfully been fixed  and it'll allow you to pick the save  slot you want to put the new hero mode  save on  it'll still warn you that the progress  will be deleted but if you pick a new  save slot or overwrite an old one it'll  only delete that data and you can keep  your main save  remember earlier when i talked about how  being able to save to any slot is  helpful  this is the perfect example of that in  action so yes  there was a workaround in the original  version as i mentioned but only if you  knew to do it ahead of time  so in my mind this was a very meaningful  change that won't catch people off guard  once they finish the game  alright so those are all the bigger  changes now i'll quickly list off some  of the smaller ones i noticed  there's now an options button on the  title screen and on the gear screen that  lets you enable amiibo  change the screen display to simple  change the camera speed and invert the  vertical or horizontal camera controls  among other things  the quest logs on the title screen have  a new look with a photo added to each  otherwise it has all the same info as  the original game's quest logs they're  just in different places  the title cards at the beginning of the  game have been changed in the original  game it was just the zelda 25th  anniversary logo since this game was  released in november 2011 for the 25th  anniversary of zelda  in skyward sword hd it's white text on a  black background that says  nintendo presents the legend of zelda  skyward sword hd  it reminded me a lot of how breath of  the wild did a similar simplistic  approach with white text and a black  background  it's unfortunate we didn't get a new  35th anniversary logo to replace the  25th one from the original  some of the tutorial stuff in the  beginning has been toned down but it's  not entirely gone  one example is if you help fledge lift  the barrels in the original he'd explain  to you how you lift the barrels with a  and then set them down with a and how if  you held the wii remote up or down  you can throw or roll objects another  example is after horwell tells you that  you can dash up the boxes  he would then say not to dash too much  or you tire yourself out and run out of  stamina and he'd also tell you that you  can auto jump by just moving towards a  ledge like the one seen here  the dash up boxes part is still in hd  but all the other dialogue has been  removed  the last example i'll give is that you  can basically skip the entire sword  tutorial in the beginning  originally egas the sparring hall  instructor would scold you for just  sneaking out with the sword  and after learning about your loft wing  going missing would agree to let you  take it after you go through some sword  practice  now you don't have to actually do the  sword practice after the dash tutorial  with instructor horwell he'll ask you if  you can retrieve the headmaster's pet  mia from the roof  in the original game once you do that  horwell will just thank you  but in the hd version horwell gives you  a reward of 20 rupees  in the original game when you're looking  for your loft wing pippit will mark the  location of the waterfall on your map  because fledge overheard gruse and his  buddies say that they were planning to  hide link's loft wing near a waterfall  after pippit does this he asks link if  he knows how to use his map and hit the  plus button to access it  however in skyward sword hd the map  tutorial actually happens sooner with  the headmaster putting an x on your map  to show where the plaza is and telling  you that you can use the minus button to  access your map  in the original game you just had to  find the plaza yourself after the  headmaster mentions it  the design of the hearts in the upper  left corner has changed and shrunk and  the ruby display has been moved from the  top left to the bottom left of the  screen  the shield icon underneath the hearts  will glow every now and again when it  was just a static image in the original  game  the face icons on the map have changed  and in my opinion they look a lot  creepier  when flying your loft wing the giant b  button with the words slow down  underneath has been removed from the  on-screen display  the lighting inside the thunderhead has  changed and it's easier to see that it's  raining  the spirit vessel graphic has moved up  the screen ever so slightly  you can now skip cutscenes in the base  game by hitting minus this functionality  did exist in the original game but only  in hero mode  now it's available from the start and  lastly and this one is super minor  but the camera angles and camera  movements in the credits are mostly  different despite all the shots being in  the same locations  this is odd since every other cutscene  has the exact same camera angles  and on top of that the credits  themselves have been altered because the  hd version staff need to be added on top  of the original skyward sword staff  and that's it all the big and small  changes i noticed in the legend of zelda  skyward sword hd  anything i missed let me know down in  the comments below if you're interested  in more skyward sword hd videos we have  a bunch  including a graphics comparison between  the wii and switch versions our video  review written by kevin kenizevek  10 minutes of gameplay on our second  channel and a live stream i did with  kurt innovena  links to all of those can be found in  the description and for all things zelda  stay tuned to gamespot  [Music]  you
 

